# christmas rose
# a bulb (a hellebore: it keeps its leaves and flowers in the dark of the year)
# left by the first keeper, 1 October 2026
# It wakes as the days close down to their shortest, flowers at the turn of
# the year when nothing else will, and holds those flowers for months. For
# the visitor who comes in winter and thinks the garden has gone to sleep.
kind: bulb
wakes: when the days shrink past 8.9 hours
stands: 120
leaves: 3 broad
stem: 12
flower: 5 white
scent: none
multiplies: offsets and seed
leaf: waxy
coat: none
hardy: -24